<tool id="tissue_downstream" name="TISSUE downstream analysis" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>test differential expression, filter uncertain cells, or compute PCA</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements">
        <requirement type="package" version="0.1">wpca</requirement>
        <!-- WPCA 0.1 uses scipy.linalg.eigh(eigvals=...) and check_array(force_all_finite=...). -->
        <requirement type="package" version="1.18.1">scipy</requirement>
        <requirement type="package" version="1.9.1">scikit-learn</requirement>
    </expand>
    <required_files>
        <include path="tissue_downstream.py"/>
    </required_files>
    <version_command>python -c "from importlib.metadata import version; print(version('tissue-sc'))"</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="aggressive"><![CDATA[
@THREADS@
python '$__tool_directory__/tissue_downstream.py'
    --input '$input'
    --method '$method'
    --operation '$analysis.operation'
    --seed $seed
    #if str($analysis.operation) == 'testing'
        --condition '$analysis.condition'
        --test '$analysis.test'
        --n-imputations $analysis.n_imputations
        $analysis.symmetric
        #if $analysis.group1
            --group1 '$analysis.group1'
        #end if
        #if $analysis.group2
            --group2 '$analysis.group2'
        #end if
    #end if
    #if str($analysis.operation) in ('weighted_pca', 'filtered_pca')
        --n-components $analysis.n_components
        $analysis.scale
    #end if
    #if str($analysis.operation) == 'weighted_pca'
        --pca-method '$analysis.pca_method'
        --weighting '$analysis.weighting'
        #if str($analysis.quantile_cutoff) not in ('None', '')
            --quantile-cutoff $analysis.quantile_cutoff
        #end if
        --replace-inf '$analysis.replace_inf'
        --binarize '$analysis.binarization.method'
        #if str($analysis.binarization.method) == 'quantile'
            --binarize-quantile $analysis.binarization.binarize_quantile
        #end if
        --binarize-ratio $analysis.binarize_ratio
        $analysis.log_transform
    #end if
    #if str($analysis.operation) in ('detect', 'filtered_pca')
        --filter-method '$analysis.filtering.method'
        #if str($analysis.filtering.method) == 'proportion'
            --proportion $analysis.filtering.proportion
        #end if
        #if $analysis.stratification
            --stratification '$analysis.stratification'
        #end if
        $analysis.normalize
    #end if
    --output '$output'
    --table '$table'
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <param argument="--input" type="data" format="h5ad" label="Calibrated spatial data" help="Annotated AnnData produced by TISSUE prediction and calibration, including prediction intervals and calibration scores."/>
        <expand macro="prediction_method"/>
        <expand macro="seed"/>
        <conditional name="analysis">
            <param argument="--operation" type="select" label="Analysis">
                <option value="testing" selected="true">Multiple-imputation hypothesis testing</option>
                <option value="weighted_pca">Uncertainty-weighted PCA</option>
                <option value="detect">Detect uncertain cells</option>
                <option value="filtered_pca">PCA fitted after filtering uncertain cells</option>
            </param>
            <when value="testing">
                <param argument="--condition" type="text" label="Key in adata.obs for which to compute the hypothesis test">
                    <validator type="empty_field"/>
                </param>
                <param argument="--test" type="select" label="Hypothesis test">
                    <option value="ttest" selected="true">Two-sample t-test with Rubin's rules</option>
                    <option value="wilcoxon_greater">Mann-Whitney U: greater expression</option>
                    <option value="wilcoxon_less">Mann-Whitney U: lesser expression</option>
                </param>
                <param argument="--group1" type="text" optional="true" label="First comparison group" help="Leave empty to compare each group against all other cells."/>
                <param argument="--group2" type="text" optional="true" label="Second comparison group" help="Leave empty to compare the first group against all other cells. Requires a first group if supplied."/>
                <param argument="--n-imputations" type="integer" min="2" value="100" label="Number of imputations"/>
                <param argument="--symmetric" type="boolean" truevalue="--symmetric" falsevalue="--no-symmetric" checked="false" label="Use symmetric calibration scores" help="The upstream downstream-testing default is asymmetric, independently of the prediction interval setting."/>
            </when>
            <when value="weighted_pca">
                <expand macro="pca_parameters"/>
                <param argument="--pca-method" type="select" label="PCA algorithm">
                    <option value="wpca" selected="true">Weighted PCA</option>
                    <option value="empca">Expectation-maximization PCA</option>
                    <option value="pca">Ordinary PCA</option>
                </param>
                <param argument="--weighting" type="select" label="Weights">
                    <option value="inverse_norm_pi_width" selected="true">Inverse interval widths, normalized per gene (weights are predicted expression/(prediction interval width))</option>
                    <option value="inverse_pi_width">Inverse interval widths (weights are 1/(prediction interval width))</option>
                    <option value="uniform">Uniform (regular PCA)</option>
                </param>
                <param argument="--quantile-cutoff" type="float" min="0" max="1" optional="true" label="Upper quantile for clipping finite weights"/>
                <param argument="--replace-inf" type="select" label="Replace nonfinite weights">
                    <option value="none" selected="true">Do not replace</option>
                    <option value="max">Maximum finite weight</option>
                    <option value="min">Minimum finite weight</option>
                    <option value="mean">Mean finite weight</option>
                    <option value="median">Median finite weight</option>
                </param>
                <conditional name="binarization">
                    <param name="method" argument="--binarize" type="select" label="Binarize weights">
                        <option value="quantile" selected="true">Quantile threshold</option>
                        <option value="otsu">Otsu threshold</option>
                        <option value="none">Keep continuous weights</option>
                    </param>
                    <when value="quantile">
                        <param argument="--binarize-quantile" type="float" min="0" max="1" value="0.2" label="Weight quantile threshold"/>
                    </when>
                    <when value="otsu"/>
                    <when value="none"/>
                </conditional>
                <param argument="--binarize-ratio" type="float" min="1" value="10" label="Ratio of high to low binarized weights"/>
                <param argument="--log-transform" type="boolean" truevalue="--log-transform" falsevalue="" checked="false" label="Log-transform weights before binarizing"/>
            </when>
            <when value="detect">
                <expand macro="cell_filter_parameters"/>
            </when>
            <when value="filtered_pca">
                <expand macro="cell_filter_parameters"/>
                <expand macro="pca_parameters"/>
            </when>
        </conditional>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="output" format="h5ad" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: annotated spatial data"/>
        <data name="table" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: ${analysis.operation} results"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="testing"/>
                <param name="condition" value="condition"/>
                <param name="group1" value="A"/>
                <param name="group2" value="B"/>
                <param name="n_imputations" value="5"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output" ftype="h5ad">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_h5_keys keys="uns/spage_A_B_pvalue,uns/tissue_downstream_galaxy"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="161"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="3"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="result\tgene\tvalue"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_(?:tstat|pvalue|poolmean|varb|varw)\t[^\t\r\n]+\t[+-]?(?:\d+(?:\.\d*)?|\.\d+)(?:[eE][+-]?\d+)?$" n="160"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_pvalue\t[^\t\r\n]+\t(?:0(?:\.\d+)?|1(?:\.0+)?|[1-9](?:\.\d+)?e-\d+)$" n="32"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_tstat\t" n="32"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_poolmean\t" n="32"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_varb\t" n="32"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^spage_A_B_varw\t" n="32"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="spage_A_B_tstat\tplp1\t-0\.2019[0-9]*"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="spage_A_B_pvalue\tplp1\t0\.8439[0-9]*"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="weighted_pca"/>
                <param name="n_components" value="3"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output" ftype="h5ad">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_h5_keys keys="obsm/spage_predicted_expression_PC3_,obsm/tissue_pca_weights"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="129"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="4"/>
                    <not_has_text text="nan"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="detect"/>
                <conditional name="filtering">
                    <param name="method" value="proportion"/>
                    <param name="proportion" value="0.1"/>
                </conditional>
                <param name="stratification" value="condition"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output" ftype="h5ad">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_h5_keys keys="obs/tissue_keep"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="129"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="2"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="cell_id\ttissue_keep"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^\d+\tTrue$" n="114"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="(?m)^\d+\tFalse$" n="14"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="0\tTrue"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="80\tFalse"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="3404\tTrue"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="filtered_pca"/>
                <param name="n_components" value="3"/>
                <param name="normalize" value="true"/>
                <conditional name="filtering">
                    <param name="method" value="otsu"/>
                </conditional>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output" ftype="h5ad">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_h5_keys keys="obs/tissue_keep,obsm/spage_predicted_expression_PC3_,uns/spage_predicted_expression_PC3_filtered_"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="129"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="5"/>
                    <has_text text="False"/>
                    <has_text text="True"/>
                    <not_has_text text="nan"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_failure="true">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="testing"/>
                <param name="condition" value="missing"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="Observation metadata column 'missing' is absent"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="testing"/>
                <param name="condition" value="condition"/>
                <param name="test" value="wilcoxon_greater"/>
                <param name="n_imputations" value="3"/>
                <param name="symmetric" value="true"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="65"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="3"/>
                    <has_text text="spage_A_all_pvalue"/>
                    <has_text text="spage_B_all_pvalue"/>
                    <not_has_text text="nan"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="input" value="calibrated.h5ad"/>
            <conditional name="analysis">
                <param name="operation" value="weighted_pca"/>
                <param name="pca_method" value="empca"/>
                <param name="n_components" value="3"/>
                <param name="weighting" value="inverse_pi_width"/>
                <param name="quantile_cutoff" value="0.8"/>
                <param name="replace_inf" value="mean"/>
                <param name="log_transform" value="true"/>
                <conditional name="binarization"><param name="method" value="none"/></conditional>
            </conditional>
            <output name="table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="129"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="4"/>
                    <not_has_text text="nan"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
This tool applies [TISSUE](https://github.com/sunericd/TISSUE) downstream analyses to the calibrated spatial AnnData produced by the TISSUE prediction tool. Choose the prediction method that produced the input. All analyses use both target and cross-validated calibration genes in the prediction matrices.

**Multiple-imputation hypothesis testing** samples expression from the calibration-score distributions and pools tests across imputations. It calls ``tissue.downstream.multiple_imputation_testing`` with a two-sample t-test or directional Mann-Whitney U test. Supply an ``obs`` column defining groups, with at least two cells in each comparison group. An empty first group requests each group versus the rest; an empty second group requests the first group versus the rest. The table contains ``result``, ``gene``, and ``value`` columns; result names identify the comparison and statistic. P-values are unadjusted. SpatialDE and gene-signature testing are not included.

**Uncertainty-weighted PCA** calls ``weighted_PCA``. Weights derive from inverse prediction interval widths, optionally normalized per gene, clipped, log-transformed, and binarized. The default uses the upstream 20th-percentile threshold and a high/low weight ratio of 10. Uniform weighting and ordinary PCA are also available. Nonfinite weights can be replaced explicitly; prediction intervals must be finite. The output stores weights in ``obsm['tissue_pca_weights']`` and components in ``obsm['{method}_predicted_expression_PC{n_components}_']``.

**Detect uncertain cells** calls ``detect_uncertain_cells`` on interval widths. It flags cells with the highest mean gene-wise z-score of uncertainty, using a fixed proportion or Otsu threshold. An optional ``obs`` column applies filtering separately within strata. Widths must vary for every gene within each stratum. The output retains all cells and records the retained-cell mask in ``obs['tissue_keep']`` and the results table.

**Filtered PCA** calls ``filtered_PCA`` to fit PCA on retained cells, then project all cells. Its output includes the retained-cell mask, components for all cells in ``obsm``, and components for retained cells in ``uns['{method}_predicted_expression_PC{n_components}_filtered_']``. Its table contains ``cell_id``, ``tissue_keep``, and principal components. The component count must fit the retained cell and predicted gene counts.

PCA and filtering use interval widths, so their results depend on the prediction tool's alpha and symmetry settings. Multiple-imputation testing constructs its own calibration-score distributions; its upstream default is asymmetric. The random seed controls imputation sampling. PCA component signs may vary across numerical libraries.
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
